= Views and Navigation

InkyCap provides multiple ways to review your knowledge from different angles: by search, by time, by connection, and by task.

Each of these is a different lens on the same notes. Use them to look something up, to write a daily log, to discover unexpected relationships, or to keep track of what you need to do.

== In this section

- #wikilink("2 - Search and Retrieval") (find anything across the whole notebox or within a single note, save searches as bookmarks, jump to a file with Quick Open, and run find-and-replace safely).
- #wikilink("3 - Agenda, Tasks, and Dates") (track to-dos and deadlines inside your notes with tasks and dated reminders, and see them all gathered in one place in the Agenda panel).
- #wikilink("4 - Journal Scroll") (how to use Journal Scroll, InkyCap's continuous date-ordered timeline feed, including sort axis, anchor scope, navigation, and daily-note pairing).
- #wikilink("5 - Mycelial View") (an interactive map of your notebox that surfaces latent links and emergent concepts, revealing where your knowledge wants to grow next).
